    "note": "Status is stored as palearctic-migrant. The research treated this as a Palearctic summer visitor, which is the same movement, and palearctic-migrant is the status this site already uses. Age-related plumage (white wing spots in immatures); no seasonal breeding plumage in Africa. Gaps: No Kruger-labelled Commons photos; European images used. Taxonomy: Clanga pomarina vs Aquila pomarina. GBIF Kruger peak Nov–Feb. Newman's: common summer visitor Nov–Mar. monthsPresent set from Newman/SABAP seasonality cross-checked with GBIF Kruger month facets (not abundance)."
